+# Unresolved decisions
+
+## Relay M5 policy ratification — TASK-260715-pa6evr
+
+The [release input contract](docs/TASK-260715-pa6evr_relay-release-input-contract.md#8-ownership-open-ratification-and-implementation-traceability)
+records concrete draft choices and alternatives for vulnerability thresholds,
+advisory freshness, exception duration, component-level license approval,
+retention clocks and immutable runner materialization.
+
+Human ratification is consolidated in `TASK-260717-2d308k`, owned by security,
+release, relay/platform and legal/compliance. No human approval is claimed.
+Downstream implementation may proceed on an agent-accepted draft; publication
+must wait for the recorded ratification verdict. No new policy task is needed.
+
+Exact M5 runner snapshots, auxiliary tools, scanners and advisory database
+digests remain to be materialized by `TASK-260715-3e7noa`,
+`TASK-260715-36gq4m`, `TASK-260715-38atsq` and `TASK-260715-nwcp1j`.
+Missing pins make a release candidate ineligible. Native Linux certification
+is deferred, not passed, and is not a prerequisite for the working-client path.
